Represents one opened cash register / POS terminal session (a work shift), controlling all sales, payments, and cash movements until it is closed.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Open a new POS session (cash count at start)
Record all POS orders and payments during the session
Cash control (opening balance, transactions, expected vs counted closing balance)
Session closing with Z-report and cash register reconciliation
Multi-session / multi-cashier operations
Handle temporary session interruptions and recovery
Generate closing journal entries and bank deposits

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
name (sequenced), config_id → pos.config (required)
user_id, start_at, stop_at
state (opening_control / opened / closing_control / closed / pending)
cash_register_balance_start, cash_register_balance_end_real, cash_register_total_entry_encoding
One2many: order_ids → pos.order
One2many: payment_ids → pos.payment (or statement lines)
rescue (boolean for recovery sessions)

Critical Hooks: action_pos_session_open, action_pos_session_closing_control, action_pos_session_validate, _compute_cash_balance, button_confirm_cash
Security: point_of_sale.group_pos_user + strict session ownership rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
POS session, point of sale session, cash register session, pos shift, session opening, session closing, Z report, cash control, opening balance, closing balance, POS cash count, pos reconciliation, session validation, open session, closed session, session state, in progress session, posted session
Related Models (most joined):

pos.config (parent configuration)
pos.order (all orders in session)
pos.payment
account.bank.statement (via cash moves)
account.move (closing entries)
res.user (cashier)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
pos.session is the Odoo model representing a live Point of Sale session linked to pos.config, with state (opening/opened/closing/closed), opening/closing cash balances, and containing all pos.order and payments for that shift. It manages cash control, session validation, Z-report generation, and automatic creation of accounting entries at closing, serving as the operational bridge between POS frontend transactions and backend accounting & inventory.